M='Bhauma / Maṅgala / Aṅgāraka in60';E='Earth personified';R='Bhāradvāja'
e,v=ev(60,'1–10','Brahmā answers the father’s question about Aṅgāraka fourth. In Avantī, learned Bhāradvāja performs agnihotra, teaches pupils and observes rites on a riverbank. Seeing an unnamed Apsaras arouses desire; he falls, and emitted semen enters an earth-hole. A red, hibiscus-coloured boy arises, whom Earth lovingly raises. At seven years he asks his mother why he is red in a human body and who his father is. Earth explicitly says Bhāradvāja’s fallen semen met her, produced him, and she raised him.',[('Brahmā',D),('Kṛtavīrya unnamed father',F),(R,S),('Unnamed Apsaras seen byBhāradvāja','PERSON'),('Bhāradvāja pupils','FAMILY'),(E,D),(M,D),('Avantī',L)],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Source-specific semen/earth origin and nurturing mother are explicit; no intercourse with Earth or the Apsaras is narrated.')
rel(M,'semen_origin_from',R,e,'SOURCE_NARRATED_SEMEN_ORIGIN');rel(M,'son_of',E,e,'EARTH_ORIGIN_AND_NURTURING_MOTHER');rel(E,'raises',M,e)
e,v=ev(60,'11–17','The boy asks to see his father. Earth takes him to Bhāradvāja, bows and presents the son born of his semen and raised by her. With his permission she returns home; the sage rejoices, embraces and smells the boy’s head, places him on his lap, and performs upanayana at an auspicious time. He teaches Vedas/śāstras and a Gaṇeśa mantra, prescribing long observance and promising desired gifts when pleased. The boy sits in lotus posture on Narmadā’s bank, controls senses, meditates Heramba and japs on an air diet, becoming thin.',[(M,D),(E,D),(R,S),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Bhāradvāja-taught Gaṇeśa mantra in60',T),('Narmadā bank in60',L)],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Explicit father’s acceptance, initiation and teacher/mantra role precede the boy’s austerity.')
rel(R,'accepts_as_son',M,e,'SOURCE_DECLARED_PARENTAGE');rel(R,'initiates',M,e);rel(R,'teaches','Bhāradvāja-taught Gaṇeśa mantra in60',e)
e_diet=e
e,v=ev(60,'18–27','After one thousand years of severe tapas, Gaṇeśa appears at moonrise on Māgha dark fourth. His arms are described as digbhuja, with divine clothes, forehead moon, varied weapons, trunk/tusk/ears/earrings, many ornaments and immense solar radiance. The boy bows and hymns obstacle removal and creation, lordship of gods/asuras, transcendent attributes and world support/protection. Pleased by tapas, devotion, hymn and courage despite childhood, the deity invites desired boons.',[(M,D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Bhāradvāja-taught Gaṇeśa mantra in60',T),('Gaṇeśa weapons in60',W)],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Exact appearance time and boon invitation; digbhuja kept as the witness term, while later image explicitly has ten arms.')
val('Gaṇeśa','manifestation_description60','60.19 digbhuja arm descriptor retained without a silent numeric expansion; clothes, forehead moon, weapons and immense radiance; installed image explicitly ten-armed60.37.',e)
e_tapas=e
e,v=ev(60,'28–31','Bhauma praises the fruitful sight, birth, knowledge, lineage, Earth and tapas. He requests residence in heaven, drinking nectar with the gods, an auspicious name famous in the three worlds, and that the fourth on which he saw the deity always grant piety, remove all distress and give vow-practitioners their wishes through divine favour.',[(M,D),('Gaṇeśa',D),(E,D),('Aṅgāraka-caturthī practitioners','FAMILY')],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Personal heaven/nectar/name requests and distinct festival efficacy request are explicit.')
e_req=e
e,v=ev(60,'32–36','Gaṇeśa promises nectar with gods and fame as Maṅgala; Aṅgāraka is explained by redness and Earth-son status. Aṅgāraka-fourth practitioners receive merit equal to a year of Sankaṣṭa observance and unobstructed tasks. The boy will become king in Avantī, and recounting the excellent vow gives all wishes. The deity grants and disappears.',[(M,D),('Gaṇeśa',D),(E,D),('Aṅgāraka-caturthī practitioners','FAMILY'),('Avantī',L)],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Requests receive specific response, plus prospective kingship and festival benefit; actual transport follows.')
p=power(M,e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',worshipped_id=names['Gaṇeśa'],requested='Heaven residence, nectar with gods, auspicious three-world name and fourth’s piety/distress/wish efficacy.',granted='Nectar with gods, Maṅgala/Aṅgāraka fame, prospective Avantī kingship; festival benefits separately registered.',austerity_or_circumstances='Father-taught mantra and air-diet lotus-posture sensory restraint; 1,000 years severe tapas; moonrise Māgha dark-fourth appearance/hymn.',notes='Future kingship not asserted as an enacted royal accession here; explicit image later ten-armed separately.')
p['evidence_ids'] += [e_req,e_tapas,e_diet];p['field_evidence']['requested']=[e_req];p['field_evidence']['austerity_or_circumstances']=[e_tapas,e_diet]
p['field_evidence']['worshipped_id']=[e_tapas]
power('Aṅgāraka-caturthī practitioners',e,v,typ='BOON',grant='Gaṇeśa',granted='Merit equal to 1 year Sankaṣṭa vow; all tasks unobstructed and wishes by recounting vow.',trigger='Perform Aṅgāraka caturthī; recount excellent vow for wishes.',notes='Year is equivalence of merit, not required duration of this festival observance.')
e,v=ev(60,'37–39','Maṅgala devotionally installs a beautiful, trunk-faced ten-armed Gaṇeśa, builds a pleasing temple and names the deity Maṅgalamūrti. The site becomes wish-giving to everyone and liberation-giving through observance, worship and seeing.',[(M,D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Maṅgalamūrti / Cintāmaṇi image in60',C),('Maṅgalamūrti temple/site in60',L),('Maṅgalamūrti-site practitioners','FAMILY')],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Actual named image/temple installation and site efficacy.')
rel(M,'installs','Maṅgalamūrti / Cintāmaṇi image in60',e);rel(M,'builds','Maṅgalamūrti temple/site in60',e);rel('Maṅgalamūrti / Cintāmaṇi image in60','installed_at','Maṅgalamūrti temple/site in60',e)
val('Maṅgalamūrti / Cintāmaṇi image in60','image_form','Trunk-faced, ten-armed60.37.',e)
power('Maṅgalamūrti-site practitioners',e,v,mechanism='All-wish benefit and liberation through observance/worship/seeing.',trigger='Visit/practice at the installed deity’s site.')
e,v=ev(60,'40–46','Vināyaka sends his Gaṇas in a fine vimāna to bring Bhauma. They bring him in the same body to Gaṇeśa’s vicinity. Narrator states he obtained heaven and nectar with gods, giving Tuesday-associated caturthī its fame. Maṅgalamūrti also becomes called Cintāmaṇi for giving desired objects; the all-obstacle-removing deity is famous west of Pārinera city, now worshipped by Siddhas/Gandharvas at moonrise and granting desired gifts, sons/grandsons and prosperity.',[(M,D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Bhauma-transport Gaṇas','FAMILY'),('Bhauma transport vimāna','VAHANA'),('Maṅgalamūrti / Cintāmaṇi image in60',C),('Maṅgalamūrti temple/site in60',L),('Pārinera city',L),('Siddhas',C),('Gandharvas',C),('Maṅgalamūrti-site practitioners','FAMILY')],story='gup4-story-angaraka',outcome='Actual same-body transport and heaven/nectar attainment close the origin/site arc; named king accession remains only predicted.')
rel(M,'transported_by','Bhauma-transport Gaṇas',e);val(M,'actual_after_grant','Same-body transport to Gaṇeśa and narrator-confirmed heaven/nectar60.40–43.',e)
power('Maṅgalamūrti-site practitioners',e,v,mechanism='Obstacle removal and desired sons/grandsons/prosperity.',trigger='Moonrise worship at Cintāmaṇi site west of Pārinera.')
